<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  What lint is told, and why. Everything lint reports is an error here
  (warningsAsErrors in app/build.gradle.kts), with no baseline. This file is
  for what is wrong for this app by design, or not about this app's code at
  all; a single place that is allowed says so where it stands
  (tools:ignore, @SuppressLint).
-->
<lint>
    <!--
      The screens take MainViewModel and hand it to the parts they draw - the
      way JemRec's UI is built, and what the screen tests rely on: they give
      the real composables a real view model that only the taps reach
      (ui/screens/ScreenTest.kt). The rule wants every screen hoisted into
      state and callbacks instead; that is a rewrite of the whole UI, not a
      fix, and a new screen should look like the ones beside it.
    -->
    <issue id="ComposeViewModelForwarding" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      Asks for @ReadOnlyComposable on any composable that calls only
      read-only ones - and asked it of the tap modifiers (recordToggle,
      instructionTap, rowTaps), whose click lambdas the compiler caches in
      slots. The compiler takes the mark there and drops the function's
      group, so those slots land in the caller's: instructionTap's came and
      went with the recorder's state (the bytecode, 2026-10-26). In a gate
      where every warning fails, each new tap modifier would be pushed to that
      mark. The 16 functions marked store nothing, and keep it.
    -->
    <issue id="ComposeReadOnlyComposable" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      These compare the build with whatever is newest on the internet today:
      a library, AGP or an API level released next week would fail a build
      that did not change. Versions are chosen by hand and written down where
      they are set (targetSdk 36: see app/build.gradle.kts).
    -->
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="OldTargetApi" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      The same, from Google Play's SDK index, which lint downloads at each
      clean build (lint-cache/*/sdk_index/snapshot.gz): a library marked
      outdated, deprecated or against Play's policy today would fail a build
      that did not change - for a store JemRec is not in (README, "Why isn't
      it on Google Play?"). PlaySdkIndexVulnerability and RiskyLibrary stay
      on: a dependency known to be unsafe should stop the build, changed or
      not. None of these is fatal, so a release build never waits on them.
    -->
    <issue id="OutdatedLibrary" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="PlaySdkIndexDeprecated" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="PlaySdkIndexNonCompliant" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="PlaySdkIndexGenericIssues" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      Found inside two libraries, not in JemRec's code: BouncyCastle's PKIX
      jar and libadb, whose TLS to adbd on the phone itself is authenticated
      by the pairing, not by a certificate authority. A trust-all manager in
      JemRec's own sources is still reported.
    -->
    <issue id="TrustAllX509TrustManager">
        <ignore regexp="bcpkix-jdk15to18|libadb-android" />
    </issue>

    <!--
      These are the app's own, each for a reason a parameter would serve
      worse: the fixed clock the screen tests draw at (LocalNow), the look
      and the dark mode every piece reads (LocalLook, LocalLookChoice,
      LocalDark), each caller's colour on the Calls tab (LocalCallerColours),
      the side panel's rows and player (LocalRowsSelectable, LocalPlayerHere),
      a bar's insets (LocalBarSides), the screen tests' invented waveforms
      (LocalInventedLevels) and ButtonPair's shrinking labels
      (LocalLabelsShrink). A NEW one is still reported, so it gets the same
      thought before it is added here.
    -->
    <issue id="ComposeCompositionLocalUsage">
        <option name="allowed-composition-locals"
            value="LocalNow,LocalLook,LocalLookChoice,LocalDark,LocalCallerColours,LocalRowsSelectable,LocalPlayerHere,LocalBarSides,LocalInventedLevels,LocalLabelsShrink" />
    </issue>
</lint>
